---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-04-23';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'April 23, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data. Optional anonymous analytics via TelemetryDeck, no game-content server.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>
    {APP_NAME} has no game server. Drawings, guesses, and game state
    travel through Messages and stay with Apple services you choose to
    use, such as Messages, Photos, and iCloud. We do not receive your
    drawings, guesses, contacts, message contents, or payment
    information.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
    <p>
      If you turn on anonymous analytics in the app's Settings screen,
      TelemetryDeck receives anonymous usage analytics from the app.
    </p>
    <p>TelemetryDeck may receive:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An anonymized installation ID.</li>
      <li>Event names, such as app launches, pack picks, restore results, and save actions.</li>
      <li>Rounded timestamps.</li>
      <li>App and device metadata, such as app version, build, OS version, and device type.</li>
      <li>Limited event metadata, such as pack IDs, counts, and timing values.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>TelemetryDeck does not receive:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Drawings, guesses, message contents, contacts, or Photos library contents.</li>
      <li>Payment information.</li>
      <li>Stored IP addresses, cookies, or cross-app tracking data.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use this data to understand feature usage, diagnose failures,
      and improve the app. We do not use it for advertising, profiling,
      or sale.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Turn analytics off</h2>
    <p>
      You can turn analytics off in the app's Settings screen. While
      that setting is off, new analytics events are not sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck GmbH processes the anonymous analytics described
      above. Their privacy policy is at <SiteLink
        href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >telemetrydeck.com/privacy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    </p>
    <p>
      App Store purchases are handled by Apple under <SiteLink
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="Apple's privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >Apple's privacy policy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Anonymous analytics are retained by TelemetryDeck under their
      own policy. Data you create in the app stays on your device, in
      Messages, in Photos, or in your iCloud account when you use
      those Apple services.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>This app does not track your online activities across third-party websites or services.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you email support or send a word report, we receive the email
      address and message content you send us.
    </p>
    <p>
      Email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>&#8288; with
      privacy questions. {BUSINESS_NAME} runs the app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time></footer>
</Doc>
